WEBVTT

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.240
And now, we bring you our
 New Year's broadcast.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.700
Kojima-san in Asakusa, 
how is it over there?

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.070
Happy New Year. We're even more—

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:26.550
Yuta, can you get me 
some tangerines since you're up?

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:30.320
It's from Shun.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.110
Oh, a New Year's card.

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.300
Why, how thoughtful. Thank you.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:44.270
<b>Happy New Year!</b>

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:44.270
<b>Thanks for another great year!</b>

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:40.150
High school boys who send 
handwritten cards every year...

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.990
are a real rarity in Japan these days.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:48.190
In a lot of ways, 
he's a national treasure.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:52.160
We know Shun will send 
us a card every year.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:56.340
You should really send him
 one on the day itself

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.160
rather than waiting to receive his.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.060
<b>Happy New Year.</b>

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:04.080
It's from Kaname.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.840
I'll bet he only sent us this 
because he was texting Shun.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:13.340
Excuse me...

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:16.840
<b>1 Unread Message</b>

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.080
Yuki-kun, aren't you going to reply?

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:19.480
It's fine, don't sweat it.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:24.640
Even if I don't text him back,
 he knows how I feel.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:25.920
You got that right.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:29.190
I'm sure he'll figure that it 
was just too much effort for you.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.800
Did you get anything from Chizuru?

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.860
No. Maybe he'll show up in person.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.280
Happy New Year!

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.510
One year ago. One year later.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.040
The train!

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.750
Hey, don't run in the street.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.120
Damn it...

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.970
Why do I have to make my New Year's

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.890
visit to the shrine with you guys?

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.230
Now, now...

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.460
It's better than lounging around 
on the first day of the year.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:30.000
We're off to a good start.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.530
Let's go wish for some good 
luck in the new year.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:35.840
I get the feeling that

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.810
luck's trying to run away from you guys.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:41.030
Hey, what are you gonna wish for?

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.800
What are you gonna wish for?

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.070
Huh? Um...

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.920
I'm gonna wish that Yuki will
leave his empty lunchbox out

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:50.670
without needing me to remind him.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:52.160
That's lame.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:54.430
Nothing lame about it.

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:57.230
Even if he does nothing else, 
that in itself will be a load off my back.

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:59.170
What are you, his mommy?

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:04.230
I might wish for world peace.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.510
Shun, the world you live 
in is always a peaceful one.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.430
It's a field of flowers.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:14.610
I came prepared.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:17.640
I brought a serious offering.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:20.440
Chizuru, you've outdone 
yourself this time.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.190
Now I can be with Mary.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:28.450
I'm a rascal for trying 
to buy love with money.

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:29.550
You mean stupid, right?

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:30.500
What?

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:36.250
What is this?

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:38.850
It's a key for a bike.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:40.310
Someone must have lost it.

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:42.260
We should take it to someone 
who works at the shrine.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:47.430
Yeah. I'll put it in here 
so we don't lose it.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.770
All right, let's go.

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:50.310
Okay.

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:52.460
What are you? Kids?

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:53.990
Candy apples.

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:55.640
When we're done.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.190
Okay, let's go.

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:03.440
Let's do this.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.730
A hundred yen!

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:08.030
But 100 yen is a <i>lot</i> of money.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:10.220
You're hesitating now?

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.640
I understand.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.150
If you don't get anything out of it,

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:17.420
all you're doing is throwing 
100 yen into a wooden box.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:20.350
You shouldn't say that.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:30.180
That guy...

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:33.420
How have I lost it already?

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:35.020
This sucks.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.620
Nope.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:43.780
Excuse me.

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:47.820
Are you looking for the key to your bike?

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:49.730
Huh? Seriously?

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:51.220
You found it?

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.340
Oh, good. Yes.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:55.830
We were going to take it to the shrine.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:06:00.830
Please let Mary and me become closer.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:04.000
Chizuru-kun.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:14.590
Hey, did you just...

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:15.290
Huh?

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:21.760
Ch-Chizuru-kun.

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:24.490
I didn't mean to! I-I put it in the 
same pocket as my 100 yen coin—

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:25.910
You monkey!

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:28.270
How can you confuse a key 
with a 100 yen coin?

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:36.690
Uh, who's this guy?

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:38.130
I'm sorry.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.290
What? Don't tell me... the guy with the bike?

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:46.010
It's fine. It's not like I need that key, anyway.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:51.750
Yeah, I'm sure it won't cause <i>any</i> problems...

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.600
Come on, hurry up.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.230
Stop dragging the back wheel.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:05.300
See? The longer I'm with you,

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.440
the further luck runs from me.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.090
Don't treat us like evil spirits.

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:11.920
Besides, it's that guy's fault for letting

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.630
Don't use words like "dropout"
 around a student

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:18.100
preparing for his exams.

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:21.140
Don't you have any tact, Shorty?

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:26.310
I didn't even know you 
were preparing for your exams.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.910
You're a third year high schooler?

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:31.910
What about you guys?

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:32.680
We're second years.

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:34.430
No wonder you look so carefree.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:38.880
You're so happy, you've got 
flowers growing out of your heads.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:39.560
No way.

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:43.220
Second years don't have to 
worry about what they say.

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:45.560
I'm even busy over New Year's.

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:49.200
You know the cram school at 
the intersection on Main?

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:50.610
Carry it there.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:53.350
The intersection past Third Street?

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:54.930
What?! We have to go all that way?

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:56.590
Don't give me that.

00:07:56.590 --> 00:07:59.220
Just be glad I'm not making 
you pay for the key.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:01.920
You gotta be kidding! You're a bully.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:03.280
Shut up.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:09.740
Hello? Oh, Mom?

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:10.460
What?

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:14.550
You want me to buy 
groceries for dinner? But...

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:17.970
No, it's fine. I can do 
it. I'll do it right away.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:24.390
Well, I have to go to the supermarket.

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:25.720
No fair.

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:27.940
Okay, take me with you.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.760
Wait, take me too.

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:30.730
Hey!

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:33.740
No one's more passionate than me!

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.780
Please take me!

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:41.370
With choices like these, I'll have to
use the process of elimination.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.890
Please!

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:44.870
Oh, my.

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:49.220
Bad luck... I've already been 
tarnished with bad luck this year.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:50.270
Yuta...

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:53.500
You guys have been acting like victims,

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:55.890
but I'm the real victim here.

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:57.140
Unbelievable.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.890
What university are you applying to?

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:02.060
Would you know it even if I told you?

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:04.230
Um...

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:11.650
Same place as my girlfriend.

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:15.410
His girlfriend! This is straight out of a manga!

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:17.310
How romantic.

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:19.530
I shouldn't have told you.

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:22.910
It's nothing like a manga.

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.160
It's not that easy.

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:28.020
She got a recommendation, so she's already in,

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:31.420
but my chances are slim.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.740
Just like a manga.

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:34.850
How wonderful.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:36.700
Enough already.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:39.180
Can the reactions and carry the bike.

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:40.930
All right.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:44.890
Let me buy you something to warm you up...

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:47.690
to make up for losing your key.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.420
I don't want...

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:51.050
What a good idea.

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:53.930
Chizuru, you've turned over a new leaf this year.

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:56.100
Of course I have.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:57.210
Wait here.

00:09:57.210 --> 00:10:00.330
Hey, wait. You don't need to do that.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.190
Sheesh.

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:04.450
Ta-da!

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:05.810
What are they?

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.000
Greeting cards.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.320
I can see that.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:12.580
I thought you were 
going to buy me coffee.

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:18.970
That's not what it means to 
truly warm someone's heart.

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:21.690
Can I borrow something to write with?

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:22.600
Something to write with?

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.810
We're going to write you some

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:30.230
What? I don't need that.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:33.980
You should accept the 
goodwill of others.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:35.730
Fine, whatever.

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.750
Okay, everyone.

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:41.040
Make sure you don't use words like "dropout,"

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:46.300
and write this: "Not 
scraping through, not failing..."

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:51.950
Oh, I know. This guy, on the brink of... um...

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:55.170
Uh, a consoling, sympathetic, 
comforting message.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:59.310
"Dropout" isn't the only word you can't use.

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:05.760
I don't have time for this.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:06.680
We're done.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.670
No, you're not.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:11.250
<b>Good luck on 
your exams!</b>

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:11.250
<b>You can do it!</b>

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:11.250
<b>You'll probably
 be okay!</b>

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:11.320
You didn't write a single kanji.

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:21.130
<b>You can do it.</b>

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:16.370
My awkward self only have
one sentence for you.

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:17.660
You're having me on, right?

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:19.060
You just decided to censor...

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:20.980
all the stuff you wrote, didn't you?

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:21.800
I did this.

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:22.640
<b>Fight!</b>

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:22.660
Those eyes are huge!

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:26.030
I don't want this.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:27.700
H-Huh?

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:31.000
Look at the time.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.430
Fine. Just carry my bike to...

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:34.910
No, no, no.

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:38.360
Please write your name
and address on the front.

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:39.090
Why?

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.420
Just do it.

00:11:41.210 --> 00:11:42.470
Man...

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:47.480
Okay, let's go put this in a mailbox.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:49.990
What? But I'm standing 
right in front of you.

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:51.440
Why don't you just give it to me now?

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.980
No, no. That's not how greeting cards work.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.540
You have to put it in the mailbox,

00:11:57.540 --> 00:11:59.910
and it'll get mailed to you.

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:03.430
I don't care about that.

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:03.720
There was one over there.

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:05.350
I don't have time to screw around.

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:05.360
Okay, let's go.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:06.390
Hey!

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:07.230
I found one.

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:09.090
What's wrong with them?

00:12:07.230 --> 00:12:09.530
Is that really a mailbox?

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:11.370
It's red. It must be.

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:13.430
No, that's a fire hydrant.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:17.620
Excuse me, is there a 
mailbox around here?

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:19.390
Move.

00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:20.630
Your bike.

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:22.150
I don't care any more.

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:25.260
With you guys around, I'll 
never get any studying done.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:26.580
But, won't that be hard on your own?

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:27.830
Shut up.

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:30.910
Are you okay?

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:31.980
Ow.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:36.980
See? We'll carry it.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:39.980
Akihiro?

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:47.110
Yuri.

00:12:58.640 --> 00:12:59.960
What are you doing?

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:02.510
Uh, nothing.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:05.790
Yuricchi, I'll be in 
the convenience store.

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:06.860
Okay.

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:11.570
You've got a leaf in your hair.

00:13:11.570 --> 00:13:13.030
What? No way.

00:13:13.030 --> 00:13:15.700
Has it been there since 
we left the shrine?

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:16.800
Who cares?

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:18.180
It suits you.

00:13:18.180 --> 00:13:19.940
What does that mean?

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:24.650
I'll be in the convenience store, too.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:29.040
Are you okay?

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:38.610
Oh, right.

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:40.770
I just went to the shrine.

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:42.920
I bought you a charm.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:45.420
Here.

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:57.900
Not even this can keep me from failing.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:00.940
What? That's not true.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:03.410
You're studying really hard.

00:14:03.410 --> 00:14:06.450
That doesn't mean I'll pass.

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:17.060
Come on, let's go.

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:19.040
Huh? Oh, right.

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:32.600
Was that your girlfriend?

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:36.970
Am I wrong?

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:38.310
Yes, she's my girlfriend.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.560
I knew it.

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:43.930
You shouldn't have said that to her.

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:45.510
What do you mean?

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:46.380
What?

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:48.240
Well, you know.

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:52.070
Shut up. Third years have 
a lot to deal with.

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:57.690
Oh, I see. You've grown 
tired of each other?

00:14:57.690 --> 00:14:59.070
Of course not!

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:00.380
Are you breaking up, then?

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:01.860
Where'd you get that from?

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:03.400
Then, what it is?

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:05.260
It's just, you know...

00:15:05.890 --> 00:15:07.610
Oh, forget it.

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:09.710
Second years wouldn't understand.

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:12.390
I'm going on ahead, so bring me my bike.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:14.810
Oh, right.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:19.640
Did you send a New Year's 
card to your girlfriend?

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:23.110
Yuri-san, was it?

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:25.690
Shut up. No, I didn't.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:29.110
I haven't sent any greeting cards in years.

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:32.410
Why don't you try sending her one?

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:35.960
Nice one, Shun-chan. You're right.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:42.050
A fresh trick like that could help 
reignite their relationship.

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:45.540
I told you, we're not 
tired of each other.

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:51.550
These guys are more trouble than they're worth.

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:54.550
Why am I doing this on 
the side of the road?

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:56.230
Write something, write something.

00:15:56.230 --> 00:15:57.600
Okay, okay.

00:15:58.810 --> 00:15:59.560
I...

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:00.890
I love you?

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.530
I wish you a very happy new year.

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:07.690
I can't write like this. Go over there.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:09.530
Hooray!

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:11.090
Sheesh.

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:18.150
<i>I don't have anything to write.</i>

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:21.750
Yukki, "Oshikura manju!"

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:23.610
Bam!

00:16:23.610 --> 00:16:26.160
Ow. That was a tackle.

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:28.990
You shouldn't play in the street.

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:31.700
Shun-chan, bam!

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:33.010
Bam.

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:36.510
Ow. What was that for?

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:38.510
<i>I never thought...</i>

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:42.790
<i>I'd end up like this in just one year.</i>

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:46.630
<i>Without knowing why I'm angry,</i>

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:52.690
<i>disappointed, or uncertain, 
I can't express myself.</i>

00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:57.110
<i>I'm so frustrated I could cry.</i>

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:01.720
A mailbox!

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:09.300
Today's mail must already
 have been collected.

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:11.560
Huh? What?

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:13.590
Well, there's always tomorrow.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:16.800
Excuse me!

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:18.950
Take this! Take our letter!

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:20.340
Please!

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:22.560
What? Hey, wait.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:23.290
Hey!

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:25.450
Mailman!

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:33.540
<i>I can't run from my uncertainty.</i>

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:36.310
<i>Nothing has been resolved.</i>

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:39.090
<i>I can't see my future.</i>

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:47.560
<i>But despite all that,
I have to keep running.</i>

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:53.090
Hey!

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:00.340
We can't catch up.

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:04.130
I didn't think I'd run so 
much this early in the year.

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:06.690
Chizuru, you're panting.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:08.340
Shut up.

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:14.380
I was shouting my lungs out while... 
sprinting as fast as I could.

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:20.500
Is that...

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:23.580
Seriously.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:29.500
You forgot... this.

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:45.150
I'm gonna die. I can't breathe.

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:47.310
The elderly are so pathetic.

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:50.060
Chizuru, you can't catch your breath, either.

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:06.200
The sun's going down.

00:19:09.530 --> 00:19:11.330
You're right.

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:13.910
You said it!

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:15.640
You said "going down!"

00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:17.390
That's a forbidden phrase!

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:22.850
I didn't say that.

00:19:22.850 --> 00:19:25.940
You most certainly did.

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:27.490
Yukki, you heard it too, right?

00:19:27.490 --> 00:19:29.760
No, he didn't say anything.

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:31.050
What? You're terrible.

00:19:31.050 --> 00:19:32.760
Shun-chan, you heard him say it, right?

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:35.440
What? Why are you asking me?

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:41.390
<i>I have to keep running, 
even if I don't know why.</i>

00:19:45.610 --> 00:19:47.830
Look. He's back.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:51.670
Hey, take this with you!

00:19:57.860 --> 00:19:59.630
Are you going home already?

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:02.470
Don't give me that.

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:04.340
I was supposed to go to cram school.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:05.920
Now my schedule's all screwed up.

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:07.510
Do you want us to carry your bike?

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:09.920
It's fine. If you guys do it,

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:12.650
I'll never get where I need to go.

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:16.270
You should enjoy yourselves while you can.

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:18.610
Once you've got entrance exams,

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:20.590
you won't have any time for fun.

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:22.530
Exams.

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:24.140
Goodbye.

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:28.260
Try to get along with your girlfriend!

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:29.290
Shut up!

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:35.980
<b>From: Uchida Yuri</b>

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:35.980
<b>Re: Thanks for the charm!</b>

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:35.980
<b>That's great. 
Let's go out when 
your exams are over.</b>

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:41.740
We get along just fine!

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:45.590
He said they get along fine.

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:49.470
He just couldn't leave 
without bragging about her.

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:51.950
What are you guys doing?

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:54.430
What happened to the bike?

00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:55.940
We sorted it.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:56.780
What?

00:20:57.280 --> 00:20:58.540
Did you buy any candy?

00:20:58.540 --> 00:20:59.600
Don't look.

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:01.970
Well, did you?

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:00.660
Shun.

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:01.550
Yes?

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:03.570
Get away from me.

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:05.460
Do you like this one, or this one?

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.920
I'm going to make Yuki write 
you a New Year's card.

00:21:08.920 --> 00:21:11.830
Oh, thank you. Let's see.

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:13.080
Um...

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:22.030
We're going to be third years soon.

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:23.940
As long as we're not held back.

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:28.470
I'll send you a card again next year.

00:21:29.540 --> 00:21:32.270
Oh, sure. Thanks.

00:21:38.510 --> 00:21:39.690
Hey, wait.

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:42.970
We went to the shrine,
but we didn't get chance to pray.

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:45.100
Oh, you're right.

00:21:45.100 --> 00:21:46.610
Okay, guys.

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:49.730
Let's pay our respects 
to the rising sun.

00:21:49.730 --> 00:21:52.850
The sun's setting, not rising.

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:55.790
Either way, it's the same 
sun. Makes no difference.

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:58.170
Huh? Didn't you know, Chizuru-kun?

00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:01.270
The rising sun and the setting 
sun are two different suns.

00:22:01.270 --> 00:22:02.710
What? Really?

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:04.400
I've never heard that before.

00:22:04.400 --> 00:22:06.890
And that's the first time I've 
seen anyone fall for that.

00:22:06.890 --> 00:22:08.470
Hey!

00:22:08.810 --> 00:22:10.760
Don't act offended.

00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:12.770
How stupid are you?

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:17.610
Maybe we should wish for 
Chizuru-kun to become smarter.

00:22:17.610 --> 00:22:18.920
I don't need your help!

00:22:19.390 --> 00:22:21.610
Okay, here we go.

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:26.900
Ready, and...

00:22:29.780 --> 00:22:31.120
One year later.

00:22:31.630 --> 00:22:32.870
Next winter.

00:22:33.730 --> 00:22:35.410
Our last winter as high schoolers.

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:42.650
The Hem of the Sky

00:24:16.430 --> 00:24:19.800
Next time: "Colorless Blue."
